WEBVTT

00:00:04.839 --> 00:00:10.789
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday the eleventh. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:12.339 --> 00:00:19.339
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, got you. Sorry, traffic on the ring road was ridiculous. Three lanes of people staring at the same cone.</v>

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:26.320
<v David Whitfield>You're better off there. The heating in the portakabin has two settings: Arctic and surface of the sun.</v>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.699
<v Tomasz Nowak>You've still got your coat on, though.</v>

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.369
<v Jamie Brennan>That's his temperature control system. Very sophisticated.</v>

00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:41.179
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a facilities review. Anything already finished we can get out of the way?</v>

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:50.060
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, tested the boiler feed pump yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished, not another one for today.</v>

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:53.390
<v David Whitfield>Good. Nice to hear something's behaving.</v>

00:00:53.869 --> 00:00:58.770
<v Sarah Okafor>And I already swapped the filter on the Palletiser yesterday. That's done as well.</v>

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:01.780
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, understood. Not carrying that one forward.</v>

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:06.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, onto what's actually needing agreement.</v>

00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:16.480
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona, can you schedule downtime for the fire panel with production first thing tomorrow? Whenever you get a chance, rather than dropping everything now.</v>

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:25.450
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, so you're asking me to arrange the downtime with production, not saying the downtime itself has to happen first thing tomorrow?</v>

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:35.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. The scheduling is first thing tomorrow. Whenever you get a chance in that bit of the morning; no need to jump on it now.</v>

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.549
<v Fiona Doyle>Fine, I'll schedule downtime for the fire panel with production first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:51.049
<v Grace Liu>Separate to that, we need someone to do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the fire panel by Thursday. It's urgent. Scheduling the window doesn't cover that.</v>

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:55.390
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Anyone able to take that sign-off?</v>

00:01:57.269 --> 00:02:00.769
<v Tomasz Nowak>Not me, sorry. I'm not available to take that one.</v>

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.879
<v David Whitfield>No, I can't commit to it either.</v>

00:02:04.439 --> 00:02:09.340
<v Fiona Doyle>And just so there's no crossed wires, I'm taking the scheduling, not that sign-off.</v>

00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:17.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. The fire panel lock-out tag-out sign-off is still unowned, then. Urgent, by Thursday, but nobody's accepted it.</v>

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Um, I'll inspect the Water Booster Pump for leaks tomorrow. That's fairly important.</v>

00:02:24.639 --> 00:02:27.789
<v David Whitfield>Leaks specifically, yeah? Not a general strip-down or anything?</v>

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:34.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, just inspect the Water Booster Pump for leaks. I'll do that tomorrow; fairly important, but that's the scope.</v>

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.430
<v Grace Liu>Okay, Sarah, clear enough.</v>

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:44.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you sort the training records for the new starters on the 3rd, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:02:46.969 --> 00:02:50.469
<v Jamie Brennan>The new starters' records only, not the whole training folder?</v>

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:56.520
<v Sarah Okafor>Just the new starters, yeah. On the 3rd, if you've got a spare minute.</v>

00:02:57.509 --> 00:03:02.060
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll sort the training records for the new starters on the 3rd.</v>

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.150
<v David Whitfield>The whole folder would need its own stand-up.</v>

00:03:07.909 --> 00:03:12.460
<v Jamie Brennan>And probably its own chair. Not volunteering for that, before anyone says it.</v>

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:22.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, while you're there, can you do a site visit at Harbour Road Warehouse with the contractor next week? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:28.810
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, no, I can't take that. I can't get away from stores for the visit.</v>

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:37.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Fi, can I hand that to you instead? Do a site visit at Harbour Road Warehouse with the contractor next week.</v>

00:03:38.419 --> 00:03:46.120
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I can take that instead of Jamie. I'll do the site visit at Harbour Road Warehouse with the contractor next week.</v>

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Same priority: it matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:53.479 --> 00:03:58.729
<v Fiona Doyle>Fine. We're leaving it as next week, not agreeing a particular day on this call?</v>

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:02.009
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right, next week is what we're agreeing.</v>

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:10.360
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah so, mine: I'll write up the near miss at the PRV on the boiler on the 3rd.</v>

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:15.189
<v Grace Liu>That's the write-up we're talking about, yeah?</v>

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:22.399
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, the write-up. I'll write up the near miss at the PRV on the boiler on the 3rd.</v>

00:04:24.519 --> 00:04:25.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Marc. Got that.</v>

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:33.699
<v Marcus Hale>And I'll take vibration readings on the turbine one this afternoon. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.209
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, you clipped out a bit there. Was that turbine one?</v>

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:44.689
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, turbine one. I'll take the vibration readings this afternoon. Not an urgent one, but it matters.</v>

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:51.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Marcus Hale on the readings, this afternoon. Full name because apparently we've got formal now.</v>

00:04:51.569 --> 00:04:55.420
<v Marcus Hale>Sounds like I'm in trouble when you say it like that.</v>

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:58.899
<v Tomasz Nowak>Only if she uses the middle name as well.</v>

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:07.750
<v Grace Liu>One still without a name: we need someone to do the pre-use checks on the FLTs next Tuesday. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:11.639
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone taking those checks?</v>

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.269
<v Jamie Brennan>Not me, sorry. Don't put my name against those.</v>

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.420
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't take them either.</v>

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:27.089
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, nobody for the pre-use checks on the FLTs. Next Tuesday, it matters but it's not urgent. Leaving that explicitly unowned.</v>

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:32.550
<v Grace Liu>Yeah. Me raising it isn't me accepting it, just to be clear.</v>

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:40.610
<v Marcus Hale>While we've got a gap, I heard a slight rattle from the AC1. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.449
<v David Whitfield>Right, an observation, not another job being handed round.</v>

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:58.430
<v Jamie Brennan>Same sort of thing: saw the pressure on the Compressed Air Dryer dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own. Nothing I'm asking anyone to do there.</v>

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, both observations only.</v>

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:08.579
<v David Whitfield>And the Waste Heat Boiler is still blocked. Can't get to the Waste Heat Boiler until production gives us a window.</v>

00:06:09.339 --> 00:06:12.839
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. That's blocked, not work we're agreeing to do today.</v>

00:06:15.079 --> 00:06:21.029
<v Jamie Brennan>Still waiting on parts for the HV board as well. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:06:22.939 --> 00:06:26.089
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, that stays blocked. No point pretending it's ready.</v>

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:40.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, the two with no owner are the fire panel lock-out tag-out sign-off, urgent by Thursday, and the pre-use checks on the FLTs next Tuesday, which matter but aren't urgent. Neither has been picked up.</v>

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:52.170
<v Fiona Doyle>And mine are scheduling the fire panel downtime with production first thing tomorrow, and the Harbour Road Warehouse visit with the contractor next week. Yep, agreed.</v>

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:57.800
<v Jamie Brennan>I've got the new starters' training records on the 3rd. Not the visit.</v>

00:06:58.779 --> 00:07:06.129
<v Marcus Hale>Mine are the PRV on the boiler near-miss write-up on the 3rd, and turbine one vibration readings this afternoon. All good.</v>

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.550
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll inspect the Water Booster Pump for leaks tomorrow. That's us, then.</v>

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.589
<v David Whitfield>Lovely. Back to the tropical portakabin.</v>

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Enjoy your holiday. Cheers, everyone.</v>
